  "@id": "https://pices-data.github.io/odis/records/zenodo-23519377.jsonld",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Polar Sea Ice Concentration & Brightness Temperature",
  "description": "This data set contains mapped sea ice concentrations derived from calibrated brightness temperature data (CBTT) from the Nimbus-5 Electrically Scanning Microwave Radiometer (ESMR). Sea ice concentration values (expressed in percent ice cover) are binned into 30 km x 30 km grid and averaged. These monthly and yearly averages are mapped onto 293 x 293 polar stereographic grids for the Arctic and Antarctic regions (90 to 50ᄀ N and S). These maps are available from the National Space Sciences Data Center on one 6250 bpi tape for Arctic data and one for Antarctic.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Mapped sea ice concentrations derived from calibrated brightness temperature data (CBTT) from the Nimbus-5 Electrically Scanning Microwave Radiometer (ESMR). Sea ice concentration values (expressed in percent ice cover) are binned into 30 km x 30 km grid and averaged.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23519378",
